    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 383 of 1991",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6367\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 383 of the laws of 1991, relating to the incor-\nporation of the New York Zoological Society, in relation to extending\nthe expiration date of free one day admission to the zoological park\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo extend authorization for one day of free admission in each week to\nthe zoological park of the Bronx Zoo set to expire July 1, 2025, to\nDecember 31, 2030\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: amends section three of chapter 383 of the laws of 1991,\nrelating to the incorporation of the New York Zoological Society, to\nauthorize at least one day of free admission for the general public in\neach week, subject to such rules and regulations as the corporation may\nprescribe, at least until December 31, 2030.\n\nSection 2: sets forth an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFor nearly 126 years, the Bronx Zoo has served as a pivotal landmark for\nthe community. It has established a learning environment for community\nmembers and forgoers across the State and Country, providing the impor-\ntance of conservation, preservation of native species, and promotion of\nzoology. This bill would allow the extension of inclusive access to all\nNew Yorkers and community members to experience the culture and academia\nbehind New York State's native species and wildlife - in this manner,\nall members of the community can experience the Bronx Zoo, not just\nthose who can afford admission. Fundamentally, one day of free admission\nserves the diverse needs of community members, expanding access to New\nYork City school groups, college students, and underserved youth and\nseniors and providing an atmosphere of educational exploration, creati-\nvity, and inspiration for all.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
